.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-SSO-ENFORCE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-sso-enforce - Turn Require SSO on or off (shows who loses access first)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team sso enforce <team> <on|off> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Turn Require SSO on or off. When on, members reach the team only after an SSO sign-in within the SSO session length, set with --session. Turning it on first lists the members who would lose access until they sign in through SSO and prints the exact command with --confirm to proceed. Open connections keep running.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	the review code printed when turning Require SSO on

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for enforce

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--session\fP=""
	SSO session length, e.g. 24h or 7d (1–30 days)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team-sso(1)\fP
